# Prime review — desk and lane current-state design
Date:2026-10-27. Reviewer:Codex Prime.
Disposition: ACCEPTED AS DESIGN INPUT with SP-01–SP-04 conditions; not a desk/schema migration.

Independent checks:0134 exact4 outputs and dedicated submission match; fresh
verify/inspect complete without mutation. All11 pinned snapshots match. Seven
worked cases parse;11 declared commit-source instances,4 explicit absences and25
cited real paths independently checked. No product code changed or suite needed.
Notes were written after the initial proposal, not first; the admitted process
deviation is retained. Do not claim that ordering was retroactively satisfied.

The three-class one-way design is useful: actual decisions/events, coordination,
then a computed view. Separating actor, executor, role and author is sound. A
fixture-only lab can be built without seating desk-coordination v2 or relocating
law-sensitive records. DEC-1/DEC-2/DEC-5 remain proposals; no real active-lane list,
canonical record or standing-seat decision is made here.

SP-01 — Review presence is not closure. Section2 currently closes a batch for any
non-PENDING review text, including held/returned-for-correction. That can hide
unfinished work. Text-only review means review present, lifecycle unresolved.
Held and correction-required stay open/blocked with attention until an explicit
resolution. Completion needs a candidate-bound explicit terminal declaration,
not prose, pointer position or the word Accepted. Correct the old W expectations
additively in the lab contract rather than testing that unsafe rule into code.

SP-02 — Facets remain independent. Publication proves bytes at a ref, not task
completion. No 'furthest facet' summary may hide an unreleased/held/ambiguous item.
Never project a live custody observation backward as a commit-time state.

SP-03 — Do not call an idle/open-multiple/unknown view a v1 assignment record with
invented none/path values. Emit a separately tagged projection, keep the accepted
canonical parser unchanged, and state source provenance. Derive over explicitly
declared fixture scope, not all historical batches or highest/latest numbers.

SP-04 — Primary matching includes origin BOOK, PAGE and BATCH. Multiple complete
matching candidates remain ambiguous unless explicit candidate-selection evidence
resolves them; no first-pointer/newest fallback. Bound review must match the
specific member/receipt candidate. Typed reviewer/actor labels are records, not
authentication or a grant. Malformed/conflicting declarations cannot become ready.

Prime decisions within this development scope:
- DEC-3: exercise explicit typed review/candidate bindings in fixtures. No new
  live record format or retroactive binding of old reviews is seated yet.
- DEC-4: future Prime-created drafts use document state only and point readers to
  the Return pointer for release/claim, avoiding duplicate stale PENDING headers.
  This editorial convention grants no release and rewrites no old page.
Next pack builds the bounded projection lab under those conditions. The pending
Grok-2 corpus remains input evidence for a later reader, not a reason to guess one.
